adType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"d7dcb62c853dcad8d7b4c8ebcad3088c76e49ca1947c5fc18179565b0e991fb9","event_uuid":"b1d9024b-039e-47b8-bd7c-b6a91355dc65","position":{"commit_sha":"d55bd40a456bf6880a78e50da95a95989fc1e45e","position":"1795447879052054001-b1d9024b-039e-47b8-bd7c-b6a91355dc65"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"818022a9bb87f2dc6af4d1fff3bb9feb0d9a83381981546aba2d0b4dca6927ff","event_uuid":"700560ff-2b04-4c30-baa9-b04786fe00d8","position":{"commit_sha":"d55bd40a456bf6880a78e50da95a95989fc1e45e","position":"1795447894299407001-700560ff-2b04-4c30-baa9-b04786fe00d8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"fb7f9d74dedc39dbdcfb444b808979c8c0625b4b26d8c2858f2cdbb836d900d2","event_uuid":"373cfa9d-48bd-4c5e-9cf4-9f130e051a91","position":{"commit_sha":"b2c8c49419095e48f4fcae0b400704125521e781","position":"1795448281929583001-373cfa9d-48bd-4c5e-9cf4-9f130e051a91"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-311_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"05f74084-8156-4489-b43f-fbb9222cdc20","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Fix committed in worktree ibisbill-notice (b0d2da19538), make verify running. Evidence: the 4 new lockout tests (generator-fails, ssm-write-fails, delete-failed-then-ssm-write-fails, interrupted) fail against the unfixed script (no notice; interrupted case exits by signal -15) and pass with the fix; 21/21 in tests/scripts/test_operator_credential_argv.py. Mutation check: removing the 'trap - EXIT HUP INT TERM' disarm makes failure-after-the-ssm-write fail. Behaviour also checked by hand on bash 5.3 and macOS /bin/bash 3.2. Doctorfish guard (tests/unit/test_review_bot_git_credential_argv.py) 31/31; make lint 0; mechanism ratchet exit 0.","timestamp":1795448281929583001}],"created_at":1795444118442762001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"871b9a2c-78de-49cd-b7d0-12116e55ba86","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"7c81-7bbf-8275-41b9"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nFound 2026-11-23 PST by the LLM-Review of Gerrit change 3535 (immoral-heated-doctorfish follow-up). `infra/gerrit/service-user.sh` deletes the review-bot's `default` Gerrit token and then has Gerrit generate a new one before it stores the token in SSM. Since 35c1983cb07 it prints a notice when the generator output has the wrong shape: Gerrit's token was already replaced, SSM was not updated, and the review-bot cannot authenticate until a re-run succeeds. 2 other failures after the delete leave the bot in the same broken state with no such notice, because `set -euo pipefail` exits silently on them:\n- `gerrit set-account --generate-http-password` exits non-zero.\n- `aws ssm put-parameter` fails (expired AWS session, missing permission).\n\nAn operator rotating the token would then see a bare non-zero exit and might not know the bot is now locked out.\n\n## Root cause\nReproduced 2026-11-23 PST against a copy of the script with PATH stubs: a failing generator (exit 1) and a failing `aws` (exit 254) each end the script (rc 1, 254) with no notice, and so does a SIGTERM during the `aws` call (rc 143). The notice lives only in the one explicit shape-check branch; every other way out between the delete and the SSM write is an implicit `set -e` exit or a signal, and no `EXIT` trap is armed to speak for them.\n\n## Approach\nFix the class rather than add more per-step branches: an `EXIT` trap prints a notice to stderr whenever the script exits while Gerrit may hold a token SSM does not. It prints only `$BOT_USER`, never `$TOKEN` or the generator output.\n- A function `arm_lockout_notice` installs `trap rotation_notice EXIT` plus `HUP`/`INT`/`TERM` traps that set a shell variable `interrupted=1` and `exit 129/130/143`. bash runs an armed `EXIT` trap on a fatal signal anyway; the handlers make the exit status explicit and let the notice tell an interrupt apart from a failure.\n- `rotation_notice` prints, for a failure: \"Gerrit's token for '<bot>' was already replaced and SSM was NOT updated; the review-bot cannot authenticate until this script succeeds\". For an interrupt it cannot know whether `PutParameter` committed (bash defers a trapped signal until the foreground `aws` returns, which may be after a successful write), so it says the run was interrupted after Gerrit's token was replaced, that SSM may not hold the new token, and that the review-bot may be unable to authenticate until the script succeeds.\n- Armed when `gerrit set-account --delete-token default` succeeds. The delete's result is captured with `if ...; then` instead of being discarded by `|| true`; its stderr stays suppressed. A failed delete (Gerrit unreachable, or no `default` token yet) has replaced nothing, so it arms nothing and the script continues as today.\n- Armed (again, idempotently) right after `--generate-http-password` succeeds, because from then on Gerrit holds a new token whether or not the delete reported success.\n- Disarmed with `trap - EXIT HUP INT TERM` immediately after `aws ssm put-parameter` succeeds, before `mktemp -d` and before step 5 installs its own cleanup trap.\nFailures keep their non-zero exit (bash preserves the status through an `EXIT` trap that does not call `exit`). The shape-check branch keeps its \"unexpected --generate-http-password output (value not printed)\" line and `exit 1` and relies on the trap for the notice instead of duplicating it. No new config key, environment variable, or flag.\n\n## Scope\n- `infra/gerrit/service-user.sh`: capture the delete's result; add `rotation_notice` and `arm_lockout_notice`; arm/disarm as above; remove the duplicated notice lines from the shape-check branch.\n- `tests/scripts/test_operator_credential_argv.py`: let the existing argv-recording `ssh` stub fail the delete and the generator on demand, the `aws` stub fail the write or signal the script on demand, and add a `mktemp` stub that can fail; add the tests below; add an assertion to the existing happy-path test `test_service_user_keeps_the_token_out_of_every_argv` that the notice is absent from stderr on success.\n\n## Testing\nAll in `tests/scripts/test_operator_credential_argv.py`, through the existing argv-recording stubs. Every new case also asserts the token appears in neither stdout, stderr nor the recorded argv.\n- Parametrized lockout test, one case per failure point after the delete: the generator prints `New password: <token>` and then exits 1; `aws ssm put-parameter` reads the token from stdin and exits 254 with an error on stderr; the delete fails (exit 255) but the generator succeeds and the SSM write then fails (exit 254). Each asserts the failing command's exit code, the \"already replaced\" / \"SSM was NOT\" / \"cannot authenticate\" notice, and (first 2 cases) that `--delete-token default` was issued. The first 2 cases are run against the unfixed script first to confirm they fail there.\n- Interrupt test: the `aws` stub reads the token, sends SIGTERM to the script, and exits 0 (the worst case: the write committed). Asserts exit 143, the \"interrupted\" / \"may not hold\" notice, and that \"SSM was NOT\" is absent.\n- No false claim, delete failed: the delete and the generator both fail (exit 255): asserts exit 255 and no \"already replaced\".\n- No false claim after the write: SSM succeeds, then the `mktemp` stub exits 1 before step 5 installs its own trap: asserts a non-zero exit and no \"already replaced\". This is the window a missing or late `trap -` would leak into (step 5's own `trap ... EXIT` would otherwise mask it).\n- Edit to the existing happy-path test: assert \"already replaced\" is absent from stderr on a successful run.\n- The existing shape-check tests keep passing unchanged (the delete succeeds in the stub, so the trap prints the notice they assert).\n`make verify` runs the whole suite, including the doctorfish argv guard, before push.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] When `service-user.sh` fails at any step after deleting the bot's `default` token and before the SSM write succeeds, it tells the operator on stderr that Gerrit's token was replaced, SSM was not updated, and the review-bot cannot authenticate until the script succeeds, without printing the token.\n- [ ] A test drives the generator-failure and SSM-failure paths through the existing argv-recording stubs (`tests/scripts/test_operator_credential_argv.py`) and asserts the notice, a non-zero exit, and that the token appears in no output or argv.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/gerrit/service-user.sh","reason":"arm an EXIT/signal trap at the point of no return so every failure before the SSM write prints the recovery notice"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_operator_credential_argv.py","reason":"failure-path tests through the argv-recording stubs"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"b1d9024b-039e-47b8-bd7c-b6a91355dc65","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"5a11-867f-8354-4172","ticket_type":"bug","title":"service-user.sh partial rotation failures lack notice","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["96cbac2a-f499-45b4-a35e-ff4714fd276f","871b9a2c-78de-49cd-b7d0-12116e55ba86","3afe3f67-5bec-44e4-a3e2-a3d5d7ac67f3","e253f17d-b5cd-479b-bbc1-5953af879bca","15eba802-9a24-4c4c-ae4b-52010cc00f7d","1fef5c34-bad8-4973-b814-04404185d98a","6529b0d7-8942-487e-acc1-0586850c0a29","b1d9024b-039e-47b8-bd7c-b6a91355dc65","700560ff-2b04-4c30-baa9-b04786fe00d8","373cfa9d-48bd-4c5e-9cf4-9f130e051a91"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795448281929583002,"uuid":"9f72b09f-1f1a-4bb7-af91-1bcbe55a166f"}